  "ticker": "TAK",
  "drug_name": "ENTYVIO (vedolizumab)",
  "drug_indication": "Ulcerative Colitis, Crohn's Disease",
  "airtable_id": 8118,
  "stage": "PDUFA",
  "catalyst_date": "2026-06-08",
  "catalyst_source": "https://www.benzinga.com/pressreleases/26/06/b53103493/u-s-fda-accepts-takedas-application-for-intravenous-entyvio-vedolizumab-in-pediatric-ulcerative-co",
  "catalyst_text": "sBLA accepted with PDUFA date in Q1 2027",
  "detailed_catalyst_text": "The FDA accepted review of a supplemental biologics license application for intravenous vedolizumab to treat moderately to severely active ulcerative colitis and Crohn\u2019s disease in patients aged 2 years and older. A PDUFA goal date was set for the first quarter of 2027, marking regulatory progress toward a pediatric label expansion. A marketing authorization application was also submitted to the European Medicines Agency for the same pediatric indications.",
  "catalyst_text_evidence": "Takeda (TAK) today announced the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has accepted for review its supplemental Biologics License Application (sBLA) for intravenous (IV) ENTYVIO (vedolizumab) for the treatment of moderately to severely active ulcerative colitis (UC) and Crohn's disease in pediatric patients ages 2 years and older. The FDA has set a Prescription Drug User Fee Act (PDUFA) goal date in the first quarter of calendar year 2027. Takeda has also submitted a marketing authorization application (MAA) to the European Medicines Agency for ENTYVIO IV for the treatment of moderately to severely active UC and Crohn's disease in pediatric patients ages 2 years and older.",
  "news_published_at": "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z",
  "open_price_gap_percent": "-0.00445",
  "intra_day_price_change_percent": "0.00319"
 },
 {
  "id": 7341,
  "company": {
   "id": 3047,
   "ticker": "TAK",
   "name": "Takeda"
  },
  "created_at": "2026-05-05T13:05:39.601937Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-06-16T13:05:46.716252Z",
  "ticker": "TAK",
  "drug_name": "TAK-881",
  "drug_indication": "Primary Immunodeficiency Disease",
  "airtable_id": 7616,
  "stage": "Phase 2/3",
  "catalyst_date": "2026-05-04",
  "catalyst_source": "https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260504944663/en/Takeda-Announces-Positive-Topline-Results-from-Pivotal-Phase-23-Clinical-Trial-of-TAK-881-in-Primary-Immunodeficiency-Disease-PID",
  "catalyst_text": "Announced positive topline results meeting primary endpoint",
  "detailed_catalyst_text": "A pivotal Phase 2/3 trial in primary immunodeficiency reported topline data showing pharmacokinetic comparability to an established therapy, meeting its primary endpoint. Secondary outcomes indicated comparable safety, efficacy, and tolerability, supporting potential for reduced infusion volume and shorter duration while maintaining flexible dosing. These results underscore clinical viability for patients requiring immunoglobulin replacement.",
  "catalyst_text_evidence": "Takeda today announced that TAK-881-3001, a pivotal Phase 2/3 clinical trial in patients with Primary Immunodeficiency Disease (PID), met its primary endpoint, which demonstrated pharmacokinetic (PK) comparability between the investigational TAK-881 [Immune Globulin Subcutaneous (Human), 20% Solution (SCIG 20%) with Recombinant Human Hyaluronidase] and HYQVIA [Immune Globulin Infusion (Human) 10% with Recombinant Human Hyaluronidase]. The study met its primary endpoint demonstrating equivalent immunoglobulin G (IgG) exposure between TAK-881 and HYQVIA as shown by a geometric mean ratio of 99.67% (90% CI: 95.10% to 104.46%) for the areas under the concentration-time profiles over one dosing interval at the steady state (AUC0-tau,ss). Additionally, secondary endpoints showed that TAK-881, a SCIG 20% facilitated with hyaluronidase, demonstrated safety, efficacy and tolerability profiles comparable to HYQVIA, an established SCIG 10% facilitated with hyaluronidase.",
  "news_published_at": "2026-05-05T00:00:00Z",
  "open_price_gap_percent": "-0.00421",
  "intra_day_price_change_percent": "0.00060"
 },
 {
  "id": 7045,
  "company": {
   "id": 3047,
   "ticker": "TAK",
   "name": "Takeda"
  },
  "created_at": "2026-04-01T13:01:37.314462Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-06-16T13:02:25.741974Z",
  "ticker": "TAK",
  "drug_name": "Zasocitinib (TAK-279)",
  "drug_indication": "Plaque Psoriasis",
  "airtable_id": 7336,
  "stage": "Phase 3",
  "catalyst_date": "2026-03-31",
  "catalyst_source": "https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260328889059/en/Takedas-Zasocitinib-Delivered-Rapid-and-Durable-Skin-Clearance-in-a-Convenient-Once-Daily-Pill-Affirming-Promise-to-Reshape-Psoriasis-Care",
  "catalyst_text": "Presented positive Phase 3 results at dermatology meeting",
  "detailed_catalyst_text": "Phase 3 data from two randomized, double-blind Latitude PsO studies in adults with moderate-to-severe plaque psoriasis were presented as a late-breaking abstract at the 2026 AAD meeting. Once-daily oral zasocitinib showed high rates of sPGA 0/1 and PASI 90 versus placebo and apremilast with safety consistent with Phase 2b, supporting a strong oral efficacy and tolerability profile.",
  "catalyst_text_evidence": "About 70% of patients treated with zasocitinib achieved clear or almost clear skin (sPGA 0/1) at week 16 in Phase 3 plaque psoriasis studies. Presented as a late-breaking abstract at the 2026 American Academy of Dermatology (AAD) Annual Meeting, these data show that convenient once-daily oral zasocitinib demonstrated rapid and durable skin clearance with a safety profile consistent with Phase 2b studies. In the Phase 3 randomized, multicenter, double-blind, placebo- and active comparator-controlled Latitude PsO 3001 and 3002 studies, more than half of patients treated with zasocitinib achieved clear or almost clear skin at week 16, a key measure of treatment success. Zasocitinib was generally well-tolerated. The safety and tolerability profile of zasocitinib in the Phase 3 studies remained consistent with prior studies.",
  "news_published_at": "2026-04-01T00:00:00Z",
  "open_price_gap_percent": "-0.00274",
  "intra_day_price_change_percent": "0.01647"
 },
